#: src/yazdir/app.py:568
msgid ""
"Printers differ in how they stack printed sheets and how a stack is fed back in. Yazdır will print pages <b>1</b> and <b>3</b> on two sheets, you put them back in, it prints pages <b>2</b> and <b>4</b>, and you tell it what you see.\n"
"\n"
"Put at least 2 sheets of plain paper in the printer."
msgstr ""

#: src/yazdir/app.py:572
msgid "e.g. take the stack as it is and slide it in, top edge first"
msgstr ""

#: src/yazdir/app.py:573
msgid "Printing pages 1 and 3…"
msgstr ""

#: src/yazdir/app.py:574
msgid "Put the two sheets back"
msgstr ""

#: src/yazdir/app.py:575
msgid ""
"When both sheets are out, put them back into the input tray <b>so that the blank sides will be printed</b>. Do whatever is easiest on your printer, keep the two sheets in the order they came out, and remember the move: you'll repeat it every time.\n"
"\n"
"Describe it in a few words (optional, shown every time):"
msgstr ""

